=== when an event engine is required (stop-loss demo) ===
need_event_for: stop-loss / limit fills inside the bar, path-dependent exits, multi-asset partial fills, capital/margin constraints checked before send.
stop_pct 0.03 stop_exits 1
nav_event_with_stop 0.820767
nav_event_no_stop 0.818344
teach: stop exits are path-dependent inside the bar; a single close-to-close vector cannot place the fill at the stop without an intrabar rule — use an event engine.
saved_plot public/p2/engines_event_vs_vectorized.png

=== library comparison (docs read this batch) ===
vectorbt: research-scale vectorized backtests on pandas/NumPy (Numba/Rust); sweep many params/assets fast — https://vectorbt.dev/ | https://github.com/polakowo/vectorbt
backtrader: Cerebro engine; write a Strategy with indicators + entry/exit logic, add data, run/plot — https://www.backtrader.com/docu/ | https://github.com/mementum/backtrader
zipline_reloaded: Pythonic event-driven initialize/handle_data API (Quantopian lineage); maintained for bugs/compat; new features → ML4T Backtest — https://zipline.ml4trading.io/ | https://github.com/stefan-jansen/zipline-reloaded
nautilustrader: Rust-native event-driven; Backtest/Sandbox/Live share NautilusKernel — https://nautilustrader.io/docs/latest/concepts/architecture/ | https://github.com/nautechsystems/nautilus_trader
ASSUMPTIONS: daily bars; MA signal; event market orders fill next open; stop demo uses min(open,close) as range proxy; Rf=0; learning only.
ASSERTS_OK
